    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0049" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.50/90: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-03T22:00:00-04:00">October 3, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1172. Your 1605, October 1, 4 p.m.<anchor n="49" xml:id="d45-f1"/> It would
                    appear that at least certain of the Ministers accompanying President Ríos
                    entertain the belief that this Government is prepared to bargain economic
                    assistance to Chile for rupture of relations by Chile. Any such belief is
                    totally in error. Our position in the premises is set forth clearly in the
                    Department’s 649, June 6, 6 p.m. The only development since <pb facs="0050"
                        n="36" xml:id="pg36"/> that time which at all bears on the question was the
                    statement that President Roosevelt made to Ambassador Michels to the effect that
                    this Government would provide Chile, in the case it severed diplomatic relations
                    with the Axis, (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) with certain additional armament
                    in order to place Chile in a better position to repel attack from Axis quarters
                    and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) with economic assistance in the unlikely
                    event of large-scale unemployment caused by the attack and shutdown of Chilean
                    mines by the Axis.</p>
                <p>It is believed desirable that there be no misunderstanding as to the attitude of
                    this Government by the President and the members of his party.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
